/*  FUNCTION NAME:      MAPROWS
    DESCRIPTION:*//**Applies a function to selected rows of an array, placing results in-place, appended at bottom, or prepended at top. fnc may widen a row into multiple rows.*/
/*  RETURNS:            array: the input with the function applied to the chosen rows, in place or appended/prepended
    PARAMETERS:
        array           (Required) A 2D array.
        rows            (Required) Index list of rows to transform; negative counts from the end (-1 = last). Order is preserved when results land in a new position.
        fnc             (Required) A LAMBDA taking one row (width n) and returning an n-column block of one or more rows. Selected rows may expand by different heights; each expands independently and blocks are concatenated.
        placement       (Optional) Where results land: (0) in place [default], (1) append at bottom, (-1) prepend at top.
        keep_source     (Optional) When placement is non-zero, keep the source rows (TRUE [default]) or drop them (FALSE). Ignored when in place.
    EXAMPLE:            =MAPROWS({1,2,3;4,5,6}, 2, LAMBDA(r, VSTACK(r, r*10))) -> {1,2,3;4,5,6;40,50,60}
    REVISIONS:          Date        Developer   Description
                        2026-06-26  Claude      Initial version
                        2026-06-28  Claude      Support row expansion (fnc returns k x n)
                        2026-11-09  Claude      Help table removed from the formula; its text is the header metadata the argument hints read (#381, #382)
*/
MAPROWS = LAMBDA(
//  Parameter Declarations
    [array],
    [rows],
    [fnc],
    [placement],
    [keep_source],
    LET(
    //  Procedure
        place, IF(ISOMITTED(placement), 0, placement),
        keepSrc, IF(ISOMITTED(keep_source), TRUE, keep_source),
        result, TRANSPOSE(
                    MAPCOLS(
                        TRANSPOSE(array),
                        rows,
                        LAMBDA(col, TRANSPOSE(fnc(TRANSPOSE(col)))),
                        place,
                        keepSrc
                    )
                ),
        result
)
);
